---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Badge from '../components/ui/Badge.astro';
import Mermaid from '../components/Mermaid.astro';
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '@/components/ui/card';
import { lastUpdatedLabel } from '../lib/build-info';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<DocsLayout title="Introduction" currentPath={`${base}/`}>
  <Badge variant="outline" class="not-prose text-muted-foreground mb-4">
    {lastUpdatedLabel}
  </Badge>
  <h1>State of State Management</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground !mt-2">
    A comparison of state management architectures across Web, iOS, and Android.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Primary Split</h2>

  <p>This report organizes the state management landscape by its primary design unit:</p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href={`${base}/store-vs-atomic/`}>Store-centric</a></strong> — state is organized around feature stores, reducers, ViewModels, or BLoCs</li>
    <li><strong>Atomic / Graph-centric</strong> — state is organized as composable atoms, providers, signals, or graph nodes</li>
  </ol>

  <p>Push and pull still matter, but they are a lower-level evaluation detail. The more useful first question is <strong>where the state model lives</strong>: in a store boundary, or in a graph of small derived nodes.</p>

  <div class="not-prose mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <Card className="gap-0 rounded-lg border border-border py-0 shadow-none ring-0">
      <CardHeader className="p-6">
        <CardTitle className="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">
          Store-centric
        </CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent className="p-6 pt-0">
        <Mermaid chart={`
graph TD
  Action["action / event"]
  Store["Store / Reducer"]
  State["Feature State"]
  Selector["selector / computed"]
  View["View"]
  Action --> Store
  Store --> State
  State --> Selector
  Selector --> View
`} />
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
    <Card className="gap-0 rounded-lg border border-border py-0 shadow-none ring-0">
      <CardHeader className="p-6">
        <CardTitle className="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">
          Atomic / Graph-centric
        </CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent className="p-6 pt-0">
        <Mermaid chart={`
graph BT
  Count["count atom"]
  User["user provider"]
  Doubled["doubled derived"]
  Greeting["greeting derived"]
  ViewA["View A"]
  ViewB["View B"]
  ViewA --> Doubled
  ViewB --> Greeting
  Doubled --> Count
  Greeting --> User
`} />
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  </div>

  <hr />

  <h2>Derived State Tracking</h2>

  <p><strong>Every state management system needs derived state.</strong> Whether state is store-centric or atomic, applications inevitably need to compute values from other values — filtered lists, aggregated counts, combined UI states.</p>

  <p>The question is: <strong>how are the dependencies between source and derived state managed?</strong></p>

  <h3>1. Automatic / Implicit</h3>
  <p>The act of "reading" a state node automatically registers a dependency.</p>
	<ul>
	    <li><strong>Jotai</strong>: <code>atom(get =&gt; get(otherAtom))</code></li>
	    <li><strong>Atoms</strong>: <code>context.watch(OtherAtom())</code></li>
	    <li><strong>Riverpod</strong>: <code>ref.watch(provider)</code> (provider rebuild + value filtering)</li>
	    <li><strong>swift-state-graph</strong>: ThreadLocal access observation</li>
	    <li><strong>Jetpack Compose</strong>: Snapshot system in <code>derivedStateOf {"{}"}</code></li>
	    <li><strong>TanStack Store</strong>: <code>createStore(() =&gt; otherStore.state * 2)</code></li>
	  </ul>

	  <h3>2. Explicit / Declarative</h3>
	  <p>The developer declares dependencies via a pipeline or composition API.</p>
	  <ul>
	    <li><strong>Verge</strong>: <code>store.derived(.select(\.count))</code></li>
	  </ul>

  <h3>3. Store-local / Manual</h3>
  <p>No dependency graph. The developer wires everything by hand.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zustand</strong>: Selectors with <code>Object.is</code> equality</li>
    <li><strong>TCA</strong>: Computed properties on State struct</li>
    <li><strong>StateFlow</strong>: <code>combine(a, b) {"{ ... }"}</code></li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>Cross-platform Summary</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 w-full overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-card">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[600px] caption-bottom text-sm">
      <thead class="[&_tr]:border-b">
        <tr class="border-b transition-colors">
          <th class="h-10 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-muted-foreground">Platform</th>
          <th class="h-10 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-muted-foreground">Store-centric</th>
          <th class="h-10 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-muted-foreground">Atomic / Graph-centric</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="[&_tr:last-child]:border-0">
        <tr class="border-b transition-colors hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="p-4 align-middle font-medium text-foreground"><a href={`${base}/web/`} class="underline underline-offset-4">Web</a></td>
          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Redux, Zustand</td>
	          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Jotai, Signals, TanStack Store</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b transition-colors hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="p-4 align-middle font-medium text-foreground"><a href={`${base}/ios/`} class="underline underline-offset-4">iOS</a></td>
          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Verge, TCA</td>
          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Atoms, swift-state-graph</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b transition-colors hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="p-4 align-middle font-medium text-foreground"><a href={`${base}/android/`} class="underline underline-offset-4">Android</a></td>
          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">ViewModel + StateFlow</td>
	          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Compose derivedStateOf, ReactiveState-Kotlin</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="transition-colors hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="p-4 align-middle font-medium text-foreground"><a href={`${base}/flutter/`} class="underline underline-offset-4">Flutter</a></td>
          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Provider, Bloc</td>
	          <td class="p-4 align-middle text-muted-foreground">Riverpod (provider graph)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
